{"id":"word:hebrew:H3058","type":"word","title":"יֵהוּא","subtitle":"H3058 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Jehu , the name of five Israelites","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יֵהוּא (H3058) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 58 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יֵהוּא (Yêhûwʼ) means Jehu , the name of five Israelites First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 38."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יֵהוּא","transliteration":"Yêhûwʼ","pronunciation":"yay-hoo'","strong":"H3058","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3058","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["יֵהוּא֙","יֵה֛וּא","יֵה֣וּא","יֵה֖וּא","יֵה֔וּא"],"morphs":[["HNp",47],["HC/Np",10],["HR/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"Jehu , the name of five Israelites","usage":"Jehu.","full":"H3058. Yehu יֵהוּא proper name, masculine (probably contracted from יהוהוא = ׳י is He , compare יֵשׁוּעַ and references; cuneiform Ia-u-a COT 1Kin 16:23 ; 2Kin 9:2 (further Schr MBAW 1880, 277, ZA iii. 3 Hpt BAS i. 296, 329 Jäger ib. 468 ); compare also אֱלִיהוּ ) — 1 king of Israel who overthrew the dynasty of Omri ( ᵐ5 Ειὀυ , A often Ἰηου , ᵐ5 L Ἰου 1Kin 19:16-17 , (twice in verse); 2Kin 9:2 36 t. 2 Kings 9 & 10 + 12:2 ; 13:1 ; 14:8 ; 15:12 ; 2Chr 22:7-8 , 9 ; 25:17 ; Hosea 1:4 . 2 prophet of Northern Israel in time of Baasha & Jehoshaphat ( ᵐ5 Ειὀυ , A Ειἠου ᵐ5 L Ἰου in Kings; ᵐ5 Ἰου , Ἰησου , A ᵐ5 L Ἰηου in Chronicles) 1Kin 16:1 , 7 , 12 ; 2Chr 19:2 ; 20:34 . 3 one of David's heroes 1Chr 12:3 ( ᵐ5 Ἰηουλ , ᵐ5 L Ἰηουδ ). 4 a Judaite 1Chr 2:38 (twice in verse) ( ᵐ5 Ἰηους , A ᵐ5 L Ἰηου ). 5 a Simeonite prince 1Chr 4:35 ( ᵐ5 οὗτος i.e. (י)הוּא ; A ᵐ5 L Ἰηου ). יֵהוּא proper name, masculine see below יהוה above.","rootNote":"from 3068 and 1931 ; Jehovah (is) He;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 2 38","keyReferences":["1Chr 2 38","1Chr 2